# LEF layer -> QRC tech file layer, Cadence format.
#
# Both stacks report 10 routing layers, but they are not the same 10:
#   LEF : M1 M2 M3 M4 M5 M6 M7 M8 M9 Pad
#   QRC : LISD M1 M2 M3 M4 M5 M6 M7 M8 M9
# Genus paired them by position, so an early run mapped LEF M1 onto QRC
# LISD, LEF M4 onto QRC M3, LEF M6 onto QRC M5 and LEF M8 onto QRC M7
# (the four PHYS-25 warnings).  This file forces name-based matching and
# PHYS-25 is gone as of the 2026-09-12 run.
#
# 2026-09-12: vias added.  Leaving V1..V9 out made Genus fall back to
# positional matching for them too, which is what produced the nine
# PHYS-129 "Via with no resistance will have a value of '0.0'" messages
# (one per via layer V1..V9) and PHYS-24 "LEF has more layers than cap
# table".  V0 is the gate/active contact, not a routing via, and QRC does
# not model it - it stays unmapped on purpose.
#
# The names below are VERIFIED AT RUNTIME: tcl/genus.tcl block 3b parses
# $QRC_FILE, collects every layer/via name it declares, and errors out
# before synthesis starts if any target on the right-hand side is absent.
# So a wrong guess here costs seconds, not a 75-minute run.
M1 M1 \
M2 M2 \
M3 M3 \
M4 M4 \
M5 M5 \
M6 M6 \
M7 M7 \
M8 M8 \
M9 M9 \
V1 V1 \
V2 V2 \
V3 V3 \
V4 V4 \
V5 V5 \
V6 V6 \
V7 V7 \
V8 V8 \
V9 V9
